"id": "neuter",
"el": "Ουδέτερα ουσιαστικά",
"title": "Neuter nouns",
"span": "A1–B2",
"blurb": "Neuter nouns in -ο, -ι, -μα, -ος and -ιμο, the odd ones such as το φως and το κρέας, and the loanwords that never change.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Neuter nouns have one big advantage: the nominative, accusative and vocative are always the same, in the singular and in the plural. **Το σπίτι** is the subject, the object and what you call out; **τα σπίτια** likewise. You only need to learn the genitive."
},
{
"p": "Most diminutives, most words for children and young animals, and most loanwords are neuter: **το παιδί** child, **το κορίτσι** girl, **το μωρό** baby, **το γατάκι** kitten, **το ταξί** taxi."
},
